  m_Name: Undoing Deletes
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: PebblePouch.Lore::PebblePouch.Lore.Entry
  _id: 4dbca313-3a0e-4190-8054-a1438a169b8e
  _createdTicks: 639304141583344858
  _modifiedTicks: 639304141632291430
  _category: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 67eb6452bf5f2224083042268f30f622, type: 2}
  _glyph: "\U0001F5D1\uFE0F"
  _subtitle: Why can't I undo a deleted Entry or Category?
  _description: 'Entries and Categories are asset files. Creating, duplicating, renaming
    and deleting them are file operations, and like in Unity''s Project window they
    cannot be undone. Lore always asks before it deletes something and tells you
    how many references will break.


    Edits of values, notes, Tags and Fields
    **can** be undone with Ctrl+Z. To be safe against deleting by mistake, keep your
    project in version control (e.g. Git or Unity Version Control) and commit regularly.'
  _sortOrder: 5
